.TH BACKUPSNAPASSOC 1 "2026-07-28" "gpfsug-tools" "GPFS/Spectrum Scale Usergroup Tools"
.SH NAME
backupsnapassoc.sh \- back up and optionally delete Spectrum Scale
snapshot schedule associations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backupsnapassoc.sh
.RB [ --delete ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B backupsnapassoc.sh
reads the snapshot schedule associations defined through the IBM Spectrum Scale
GUI and writes to standard output a runnable
.B bash
script that recreates them. Redirect that output to a file so the associations
can be re-applied later \(em for example around a software upgrade, during which
.BR mmcrsnapshot (1)
and
.BR mmdelsnapshot (1)
activity must be quiesced.
.PP
The associations are read with
.I lssnapassoc
and recreated with
.I mksnapassoc
from the GUI CLI directory
.IR /usr/lpp/mmfs/gui/cli .
If the command is not run as
.BR root ,
each GUI CLI invocation is prefixed with
.BR sudo .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --delete
After emitting the re-apply commands, also delete every existing snapshot
schedule association (via
.IR rmsnapassoc ).
Always capture the standard output first so the associations can be restored.
The delete arguments are passed to
.I rmsnapassoc
as a fixed argument list, so values originating from GUI output are never
interpreted as shell syntax.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred while deleting a snapshot association. The offending command
is printed to standard error so it can be re-run manually.
.TP
.B 2
No snapshot schedule associations were found; nothing to do.
.SH EXAMPLES
Back up all associations:
.PP
.RS
.EX
\&./backupsnapassoc.sh > snapassocs.sh
.EE
.RE
.PP
Back up and then delete them (run before an upgrade):
.PP
.RS
.EX
\&./backupsnapassoc.sh --delete > snapassocs.sh
.EE
.RE
.PP
Re-apply them (run after the upgrade):
.PP
.RS
.EX
\&./snapassocs.sh
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lpp/mmfs/gui/cli/lssnapassoc
Lists existing snapshot schedule associations.
.TP
.I /usr/lpp/mmfs/gui/cli/mksnapassoc
Creates a snapshot schedule association.
.TP
.I /usr/lpp/mmfs/gui/cli/rmsnapassoc
Removes a snapshot schedule association.
.SH AUTHOR
Achim Christ.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmcrsnapshot (1),
.BR mmdelsnapshot (1)
